  "final_message": "The bug was in `collect` in `billing/payments.py`. When a customer had no default payment method, it returned `None` without recording a failure. So `record_failure` never ran. That meant no attempt was counted, no retry was scheduled, no `invoice.payment_failed` event was emitted, and the subscription never went `past_due`.\n\nThe fix is one call before that return: `record_failure(ctx, invoice, \"no_payment_method\")`. A missing payment method now goes through dunning the same way an expired card already did. The docstring already said it should.\n\nThe existing 24 tests pass. I didn't add a test for the no-payment-method case, and I didn't run a no-payment-method scenario by hand either.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` as `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.",
